master node runs all the management software

the scheduler does scheduleany worker pods on mater node
because when a kubernetes cluster is first set up, a taint is set on master node automaytically that prevents any pods from being scheduled on this node

you can see this and modify this behaviour if requires(best practice is not to deploy any applications on master node)

to see this taint
run: kubectl describe node node_name | grep Taint

run: kubectl describe node kubemaster | grep Taint
