Common Use Cases

• Dedicated Nodes: Reserve specific nodes for a particular team, project, or workload type.
• Special Hardware: Keep standard pods off nodes equipped with expensive GPUs, FPGAs, or high-speed SSDs.
• Node Maintenance & Health: Kubernetes automatically adds built-in taints (like node.kubernetes.io/unreachable) to evict pods when a node fails or runs out of disk space.

